nit: In the rest of the file we comment the motivation behind a particular `if` block before the if-statement, not inside of it. This comment applies to all occurrences in the PR.

 Consider:

```suggestion
             // Cannot change private flag on existing broker
            if (tx.isFlag(tfLoanBrokerPrivate))
            {
                return temINVALID;
            }
```

If somehow the preclaim of preflight checks fail, this code would allow setting a domainID to a public LoanBroker. 

I suggest the following:

```suggestion
        if (ctx_.view().rules().enabled(fixLendingProtocolV1_1))
        {
            if (tx.isFlag(tfLoanBrokerPrivate))
            {
                broker->setFlag(lsfLoanBrokerPrivate);
                if (auto domainID = tx[~sfDomainID])
                    broker->setFieldH256(sfDomainID, *domainID);
            }
        }
```

There might be an issue here. With the current logic, we would be updating the DomainID at every call to LoanBrokerSet. DomainID should only be updated when the DomainID field is provided in the transaction. If the `DomainID` is provided, and is empty, the `LoanBroker.DomainID` should be cleared.

Also, this logic should be amendment gated. I understand, that we perform amendment gating prior, but again the spirit of defensive programming.

```suggestion
        if (ctx_.view().rules().enabled(fixLendingProtocolV1_1) &&
            broker->isFlag(lsfLoanBrokerPrivate))
        {
            if (auto const domainID = tx[~sfDomainID])
            {
                if (*domainID != beast::zero)
                {
                    broker->setFieldH256(sfDomainID, *domainID);
                }
                else if (broker->isFieldPresent(sfDomainID))
                {
                    broker->makeFieldAbsent(sfDomainID);
                }
            }
        }
```

Let's amendment gate this. This should not run, under any circumstance if the amendment is disabled. Also, [as per our discussion ](https://github.com/XRPLF/XRPL-Standards/pull/484/changes#r2912419048) we should fail the transaction if DomainID is set, and the LoanBroker is not private.


```suggestion
        if (ctx.view.rules().enabled(fixLendingProtocolV1_1))
        {
            if (sleBroker->isFlag(lsfLoanBrokerPrivate) && domainID)
                return tecNO_PERMISSION;
        }
```

Invariant only enforces one direction: `DomainID present → private flag set`. The reverse (`private flag set → DomainID present`) is not checked, so a private broker without a DomainID won't trigger a failure. Add the complementary check:

```suggestion:0+7
            JLOG(j.fatal()) << "Invariant failed: DomainID is set on public Loan Broker";
            return false;
        }

        if (after->isFlag(lsfLoanBrokerPrivate) && !after->at(~sfDomainID))
        {
            JLOG(j.fatal()) << "Invariant failed: private Loan Broker has no DomainID";
            return false;
```

Design gap: private broker can be created without `DomainID`, but `LoanSet::preclaim` rejects loans against such brokers (`tecNO_AUTH`). Users can burn reserves creating a permanently unusable broker. Should `tfLoanBrokerPrivate` require `sfDomainID` to be present?

Consider adding:
```cpp
if (tx.isFlag(tfLoanBrokerPrivate) && !domainID)
    return temMALFORMED;
```

